cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FlowTopo: orderings, layerings and kernels for D8 flow networks"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jiang
    given-names: Lulu
    affiliation: "Sun Yat-sen University"
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Huan
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Weitian
  - family-names: Huang
    given-names: Zhijun
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Ting
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Lingfeng
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hellolulujiang/flowtopo"
abstract: >-
  Reusable structures for a D8 flow network: three serial orderings, three
  parallel layerings and two spatial partitions, computed once from the
  flow-direction grid. Four kernels exercise them under every propagation
  manner each supports. The conflict-free downstream layering guarantees that
  no two cells in a layer share a receiver, which makes a threaded push safe
  without atomics and is the only way to run Strahler stream order under push
  at all.
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - flow direction
  - drainage network
  - parallel algorithms
references:
  - type: software
    title: "pyflwdir: fast methods to work with hydro- and topography data in pure Python"
    authors:
      - family-names: Eilander
        given-names: Dirk
        affiliation: "Deltares; Institute for Environmental Studies (IVM), Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Deltares/pyflwdir"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.4287337"
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      FlowTopo's flat downstream-pointer representation, its D8 decoding
      conventions, its donor-count array and its breadth-first sequence builder
      follow this package.
